title start
kind: default
tags: notation tutorial
AIU notation in one page
title end

paragraph start
Files end in .aiu. Everything sits inside a named block: a line with the name and the word start, the content, then a line with the name and the word end. Markers sit alone on their line, at column 0, in lowercase. Text outside a block is an error. Never type numbers, the viewer computes section numbers.
paragraph end

section start
title start
Blocks
title end
paragraph start
The blocks are title, paragraph, section, code, comment and answer. A file starts with a title. A section starts with its own title, then holds paragraphs, code, comments and other sections. Paragraphs are plain prose only: no bold, italic, links, lists or tables.
paragraph end
code start
language: text
title start
tags: demo
My page
title end

section start
title start
A section
title end
paragraph start
Plain text goes here.
paragraph end
section end
code end
section end

section start
title start
Declarations
title end
paragraph start
A declaration is a keyword, a colon and a value, written directly under the start line of its block.
paragraph end
code start
language: text
tags: a b c              file title
kind: plan               file title, picks the file type
language: racket         code block
style: bold dim italic   paragraph or title
color: red green blue    paragraph or title
todo: description        any block
for: ID                  answer
asked: question text     answer
code end
section end

section start
title start
Todo marks
title end
paragraph start
A todo line puts a TODO badge in the top-right corner of the block and hangs the description under it. Start the description with the word done and the badge reads DONE.
paragraph end
code start
language: text
paragraph start
todo: write the install guide
Install the tool on a clean machine.
paragraph end
code end
section end

section start
title start
Comments
title end
paragraph start
A comment inside a block belongs to that block. A comment around several blocks covers all of them. Each is drawn as its own box.
paragraph end
code start
language: text
paragraph start
The text of the block.
comment start
A note about this block.
comment end
paragraph end
code end
section end

section start
title start
File types
title end
paragraph start
kind under the file title picks a type. The checker then rejects blocks the type forbids, demands its sections in order and applies its contracts. Types: decision, plan, research, module, note, book, journal, todo, default. A note allows no sections. The default type allows everything.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Questions and answers
title end
paragraph start
Each type asks questions about its blocks, shown under the block. An answer block goes inside the block it judges and is matched to its question by ID. The asked line keeps a copy of the question, so a reworded question shows as STALE and nothing is rewritten.
paragraph end
code start
language: text
paragraph start
Install the tool and run the checker.
answer start
for: qadd5fe
asked: Is this one action that can be finished and checked?
Yes. One install and one check.
answer end
paragraph end
code end
section end

section start
title start
Commands
title end
code start
language: text
aiu check FILE     list every error with its line
aiu see FILE       draw the page as boxes
aiu new TYPE FILE  start a page from a type
aiu fill FILE      add an empty answer under every question
aiu list           show the blocks and types
code end
paragraph start
Fix one error at a time from the top, because later ones often disappear.
paragraph end
section end
